# Fintech Platform – System Design

## Overview

This document describes the high-level architecture of the fintech web platform built with:

- Next.js 16
- TypeScript
- PostgreSQL
- Prisma ORM
- MVC + Service Layer Architecture

The platform provides:

- mobile wallet payments
- cross-wallet transfers
- transaction ledger
- webhook processing
- virtual card funding

Wallet integrations include:

- M-Pesa
- EcoCash
- MTN MoMo
- Airtel Money

---

# High Level Architecture

User interacts with the web app which communicates with backend services.

Frontend, API routes, and backend logic run in the same Next.js application.

Architecture layers:

View → Controller → Service → Repository → Database

---

# System Architecture Diagram

User Browser
    ↓
Next.js Frontend (App Router)
    ↓
API Routes
    ↓
Controllers
    ↓
Services
    ↓
Wallet Adapters
    ↓
External Wallet APIs

Database operations are handled through repositories.

---

# Application Layers

## View Layer

Responsible for UI rendering.

Location:

src/app/

Example pages:

- dashboard
- send-money
- wallets
- transactions

Example file:

app/send-money/page.tsx

Responsibilities:

- render forms
- display wallet balances
- show transaction history

---

## Controller Layer

Handles HTTP requests.

Location:

src/controllers/

Examples:

payment.controller.ts  
transfer.controller.ts  
wallet.controller.ts  

Responsibilities:

- validate request
- call service layer
- return responses

Example flow:

API Route → Controller → Service

---

## Service Layer

Contains business logic.

Location:

src/services/

Examples:

payment.service.ts  
transfer.service.ts  
wallet.service.ts  
ledger.service.ts  

Responsibilities:

- wallet orchestration
- transaction validation
- payment processing
- ledger recording

Services should not depend on HTTP logic.

---

## Wallet Adapter Layer

External APIs are isolated via adapters.

Location:

src/services/wallets/

Adapters:

mpesa.adapter.ts  
ecocash.adapter.ts  
mtn.adapter.ts  
airtel.adapter.ts  

Responsibilities:

- call wallet APIs
- normalize responses
- handle retries

Example responsibilities:

initiatePayment()  
verifyPayment()  
sendPayout()

---

## Repository Layer

Handles database operations.

Location:

src/repositories/

Examples:

user.repository.ts  
transaction.repository.ts  
ledger.repository.ts  

Responsibilities:

- database queries
- persistence
- transaction safety

Uses Prisma ORM.

---

# Database

Database used:

PostgreSQL

ORM:

Prisma

Main tables:

users  
wallets  
transactions  
ledger_entries  
cards  

Ledger table acts as the financial source of truth.

